# BuildKit uses THIS file (next to the Dockerfile) instead of the root .dockerignore for
# `docker build -f deploy/lite/Dockerfile.lite .`. The root one is tuned for the meeting-api build
# and excludes clients/ + **/dist/ — but the lite image builds the dashboard (clients/dashboard +
# packages/transcript-rendering/dist) and the bot workspace (core/), so we KEEP those while still
# dropping the heavy/irrelevant trees (node_modules, venvs, caches).
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.turbo
.git
*.log
.DS_Store
.recordings
**/.recordings
.env
.env.*
deploy/execution-targets.json
# Optional operator-supplied native meeting SDK (P17, ADR-0039): its archive, headers, libraries,
# bundled Qt and the compiled wrapper are operator files. They never enter git or an image build
# context, even when a local checkout holds them. Everything under native-meeting/native/ is denied
# unless re-included by name below.
# >>> native-sdk-exclusion (P17 · ADR-0039 · byte-identical in .gitignore, .dockerignore, deploy/lite/Dockerfile.lite.dockerignore; scripts/parity.json · gate:vendor-payload)
core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/native/*
!core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/native/README.md
!core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/native/binding.gyp
!core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/native/zoom_wrapper.cpp
core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/**/zoom_meeting_sdk
core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/**/sdk
core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/**/build
core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/**/*.node
core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/**/*.so
core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/**/*.so.*
core/meetings/services/bot/runtime/native-meeting/**/*.tar.*
# <<< native-sdk-exclusion
